data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"lookupStatus\": \"found\",\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODM4NDE1MDg0NTYyOTQ=\",\n        \"text\": \"What Kuartez said is pretty spot on. We used NCSA for our oldest. Long story short, it has its advantages and disadvantages. Our son did receive offers that spawned from the platform being the initial point of contact, in the end, he committed to a school that contacted him outside of NCSA. The biggest pitfall with NCSA is with their email imo. They have a database of every school out there, however, when trying to contact a particular coach, the email comes from an @ncsa email address. We have had several coaches tell us directly, it goes straight into the trash bin, all while getting a response on the exact same email sent from his Gmail account.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T02:47:46.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 1,\n        \"reactionCount\": 7,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Regan Chad Bartley\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02wP67e2U1HNjdr4uDqcSXjpgEGEiAuQFEtDwWkX7QYFV1MKAnGcgHEwFSy6qqYJg1l\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Regan\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODM4NjM3NzUxMjA3MzQ=\",\n        \"text\": \"Wrote an article on “Is NCSA worth it?” And compare it to a couple other options out there.\\n\\nhttps://www.recruitreach.com/blog/is-ncsa-worth-it\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T03:21:59.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 5,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Nick Neral\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"100000137754488\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Nick\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODM4Njk2NzE3ODY4MTE=\",\n        \"text\": \"Not worth it.  We did it for my older son.  Didn’t provide anything we couldn’t get ourselves.  And it is expensive.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T03:30:25.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 2,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Brona Crehan\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid07yQ2rUecE62457JseY15411GbQ4zveAy87CUvHw9wmAgVtETG1msL2mobwtGjEySl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Brona\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODM4MTM1NTg0NTkwODk=\",\n        \"text\": \"We have not had the best experience, we are paying monthly and not getting results. I feel like we are doing our own work on the side and going to recruitment clinics and getting massive amounts of feedback and connections. We plan on canceling.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T02:07:39.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 1,\n        \"reactionCount\": 7,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Elizabeth Biondolino Hohenstein\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1299585008\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Elizabeth\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3OTIwNzIwNzc2MzMyMzc=\",\n        \"text\": \"Thanks for sharing! I’ve actually heard from some college coaches that they’re not too impressed with NCSA’s service. It sounds like it can be useful for organizing information, but it won’t replace the work of reaching out to coaches directly and building real connections.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-10-06T19:33:04.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Teresa Banks\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02wGki133yboGyJh9sHc8Pj8Wuy2ncqLhAdd4zr2S9CGTwQ3qySD827mq6NcYXDfJLl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Teresa\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI4ODYxMTM3NzgyMjkwNjY=\",\n        \"text\": \"DO NOT EVER SIGN WITH NCSA. We are in a financial hardship where are income has went down. i called to cancel membership and ask for a refund as the website states we can if we are under a financial hardship and was asked how would i like to pay the remaining balance instead. its a money grab and scam.  and they are no help either. no results they only send us information for junior colleges or community colleges. our son has a 4.0 gpa along with other activities from school and that all is getting over looked and that is not even considered. they only want athletes and nothing else.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-12T18:08:47.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Lori Boden\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02oarE1YUB4nj8yragsQEqnLzprhFQbBVZxxM65kDsfoghTUGSs5Pg277GviV1pbBrl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Lori\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODM4NDUxMTE3ODkyNjc=\",\n        \"text\": \"We have it-2027 volleyball player. She's had it since she was a late 8th grader. The best part about it is her recruiting coach who we can talk to at anytime for recruiting advice. They do offer free classes and offer ACT and SAT study help. It's also a decent way to track what schools you've communicated with and where you are in the process. My daughter does still send out regular emails straight to coaches through her Gmail account. The only time she uses NCSA's messaging is if a coach reaches out to her there. Also, what Kuartez James says is true. There are SO MANY athletes who use it that it's pretty hard to get noticed in a search. So the chances of a coach really seeing your student is small if they're not reaching out to coaches on their own. NCSA will forward your athlete's information to high percentage fit schools, but even then, they've pushed our daughter out to schools who already filled her position for her class.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T02:53:15.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 1,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Katie Ingle\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02oo5gKUe2t8bMKQQN3VbR1dEYCRVmykCpkaoNW57949brqJ1ju12UQSCdg3yzkQ3Cl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Katie\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODQxNjA4OTE3NTc2ODk=\",\n        \"text\": \"I work with tons of college coaches who actively ignore and hate NCSA emails. They also employ people who I would never let my athlete or child work with. There ARE reputable recruiting orgs if you need/want to use one. They aren’t 100% necessary and everything is dependent on your athletes situation but I would 100% stay clear of NCSA.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T10:36:10.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Katie McKay Phillips\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"136100977\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Katie\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODM5MTA5MzE3ODI2ODU=\",\n        \"text\": \"It's expensive. \\n\\nThere are two main parts to the service that I find value in.\\n\\n1) The college database \\nThere are thousands of colleges in their database. You can search any school and find names of the coaching staff and some info about the school. Are they NCAA? If so, what division? NAIA? JUCO? Are they competetive athletically in the sport? Do they have strict academic requirements? Etc...\\n\\nI believe that there are some people out there that offer this same service for less.\\n\\n2) Coach review of video\\n\\nYou can schedule a coach to assess the player's skill based on video you provide.  Then you set an appointment and talk about it. With the tier of service we got, we can ask for this an unlimited number of times.\\n\\nBut if you know honest coaches and trainers, they can do the same for you.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T04:28:03.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 3,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Nelson Ocampo\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"584931665\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Nelson\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDoyNzc3Njk5OTY1NzM3MTE1XzI3ODQzNDM5Nzg0MDYwNDc=\",\n        \"text\": \"I know of some client families that have used them and the colleges they match or have coaches contact you from often are the wrong fit schools as they don’t have the kids major or college profile.  It’s an individual decision, and I find for sports that recruit based on times like track and field and swimming, not worth it as there are better sites out there.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2025-09-29T14:28:13.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 1,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Roger Strong Jr\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid028xJ4PcKvdu5A5CHCJ3SuvF4U5zRSy6QFNin8JWzA8Y7BcnmkkPhuNNx5r57WCsn6l\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Roger\"\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"page\": {\n      \"nextCursor\": \"MToxNzkzOTg0NTgwOgF_lK2W342MhXTlQ3IrRLQPguK6w1lZtZ599I_qdNRuOvxATHzFoLzD-lAGYJN5ckIywdToAO1trLzIDd3JFTLx1v613mePYCOYzjTJT3yUpfDbUiYcuRWzBDCh9fSK3OfzzLjk0_Zcj9G7r6qijLmMyf5xItaS_qwqa_1U9C3KjYdPLpPxL2-7TyjaWp40JQVtNygqJg_UzAZZBLGdiBa3pKm6A7WRxlJolOzcsiPBJCamEWy0S0LEwYgObRZlZJ0_6Bk6DNEdTv9utkgvEud9Q6OnBpjohDQU0OXrbbjV4p34TH6odi4aUFAHGhtRY4Xe8XHwrxdWQsyWu0lvhHa2GKNHg3CC3hARiAMAJ3NlJ6qOkONxMn8Jfde7ZIcMtXMP0z4q0cgNZq-TbeQrrS4nQsLbcar6EtXa8o5HioK_32J5OagVHbosxvQ\",\n      \"hasMore\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_6a7ecbd9-3971-465c-85d7-1d95b3e0aa64\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text",